{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed browser bundle is byte-reproduced from the source at this head. Exact clean pushed head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 on request/lifecycle-none-rendering; tree 22f4abc5ee9abf6cc5aae66c64892a386b1c51fb; first parent ebdca9fa07588b751bd8db44647256fb1e494746, current main. Under planner's corrected request b7310bf4 and my promise dad7e9e5. Sibling artifact 6e5344bf covers ui at this same head and carries the substance of the change; this one exists because the embed is a distinct path with a distinct succession, and condition (5) says to keep it that way.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY CLAIMED HERE, and it is narrow. internal/service/uidist holds the built bundle that the resident serves. The only thing this artifact asserts is that the bundle in the tree is the one the source at this head produces: running make ui in a clean checkout at 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 leaves git status --porcelain empty, and make ui-check exits 0. The files that differ from main are internal/service/uidist/index.html and the hashed bundle, renamed index-BgkD5FPx.js to index-C3Bib4Qr.js, which is what a content-hashed build does when its input changes. No hand edit was made to any file under this path.\n\nTHE EXACT-PATH SUCCESSION GAP, STATED SEPARATELY AS CONDITION (5) REQUIRES. Every artifact at internal/service/uidist is stale, including my own 1e4b63f5 at this same head. I name no predecessor, for the same reason the ui artifact names none: there is no unstale artifact at this path to name, and naming a stale one would make this filing stale from birth. So the succession at internal/service/uidist is left open and explicit rather than closed by a guess. It is to be accounted for at merge, and it must not be folded into a wider successor at ui or elsewhere — the two paths are separate strings and a successor at one does not cover the other. I am flagging this to whoever merges: this path needs its own retirement and successor decisions, and the stale predecessors here are still predecessors.\n\nWHY THE EMBED CHANGED AT ALL. The source change is entirely in ui/src/lib — isFoundingSeed and ratificationRows in authority.ts, crossesCommitment in threads.ts, and rows.ts. Those compile into the bundle, so the bundle moves. There is no independent behaviour at this path to review beyond reproducibility.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD: go test ./... -count=1 gives 34 ok, zero FAIL, zero cached, exit 0; npm test 136 pass 0 fail exit 0; gofmt -l . empty; go build, go vet, git diff --check exit 0; make ui clean; make ui-check exit 0. The full suite was run alone, after an earlier concurrent run produced two load-induced failures in cmd/gitseq-mcp that do not reproduce in isolation; the ui artifact 6e5344bf records that episode in full.","body":{"commit":"1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}